{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a4268fe12c2a5f9fcd4da8d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-2csj4k"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Pin tested runtime peers in the published manifest so Bun installs resolve them without peer-range warnings"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Bun resolves a bundled package's dependencies from the registry instead of using bundleDependencies. Since @opentelemetry/api 1.10.0 was published on 2026-10-20, bun add and first-run bunx of every pm release print four 'warn: incorrect peer dependency \"@opentelemetry/api@1.10.0\"' lines: @sentry/node 10.76.2 asks for ^1.9.1, Bun picks the newest 1.10.0, and the OpenTelemetry 2.12 packages in the tested closure cap their peer below 1.10.0. Runtime is unaffected because Node resolves the bundled 1.9.1 inside the package, but the install output looks broken and Bun downloads an untested peer set. Measured on 2026-11-01 with fresh caches: 2026.10.31 and 2026.11.1 both print four warnings; repacking 2026.11.1 with the tested peer pinned as a bundled dependency prints none (control: the unmodified repack still prints four). npm, npx and the bundled runtime closure (pm-gh1417) are unchanged. Sentry 11 would drop these OpenTelemetry packages but is blocked separately on pm-t3jxjj."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","bun","dependencies","packaging"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The published manifest pins every non-optional peer target of the runtime ledger to its ledger version and bundles it; Optional-only peers and peers already declared as direct dependencies are left unchanged; The packed-artifact smoke installs the tarball with a plain bun add and fails on any peer-range warning; npm/npx runtime verification and the bundled closure are unchanged"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"In an empty project with a fresh BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR run bun add @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.1 and read stderr."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Bun installs of the published package resolve every required peer of the tested closure to its tested version and print no peer-range warnings."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"bun add @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.1 prints four incorrect peer dependency warnings for @opentelemetry/api@1.10.0."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.11.1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"packaging"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7zs0","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1417","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_so